The source confirms the IRQ3 bug, but two premises need qualification. The deassert handler leaves IRQ3 unchanged when another line is pending; it does not fully recompute the output. Also, the UART has a path where clearing `MCR.IENABLE` leaves its line asserted despite having a deassert call elsewhere, so the call-count census does not prove every clearing path works.
